.TH CLAYMORE-GUI 1 "September 2026" "rog-claymore-linux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claymore-gui \- lighting control for the ASUS ROG Claymore
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claymore-gui
[
.B \-\-tray
|
.B \-\-window
] [
.B \-\-no\-design
]
.br
.B claymore-gui
.B \-\-export-icons
.I directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
The GTK 3 interface for the ASUS ROG Claymore: an animated preview of the
firmware effects, a per-key design editor, the sync server and a panel icon
that keeps a design applied with the window closed.
.PP
It needs GTK 3 at run time and, unless it finds no keyboard, the same access to
.I /dev/hidraw
that
.BR claymore (1)
needs.
.SH TABS
.SS Effects
A gallery of the firmware effects with a live preview, and speed, brightness,
direction, random and colour controls. Applying an effect writes it to the
keyboard's flash, which is what makes it stick; there is no way to display an
effect without committing it, so nothing here is a preview-only setting.
.SS Design your own
Paint keys with the brush, copy a key's colour with the eyedropper, middle
click to erase, fill everything or start from a rainbow. The first edit puts the
design on the keyboard by itself and it stays there after the window closes;
the keyboard keeps the last frame it is given, so nothing has to keep running.
Unticking
.I Show on keyboard
hands the board back to its own effects.
.PP
Designs are saved under a name in
.IR ~/.config/claymore/designs/ .
.I Save
overwrites the current one and
.I "Save as..."
names it.
.I "Load at startup"
marks one to be loaded every time the program starts, and it is the same design
that
.B "claymore paint --default"
applies at login.
.SS Sync
Start the socket server and watch what arrives; see
.BR "claymore syncd" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start with the window hidden and only the panel icon shown, whatever the
.BR start\-in\-tray
setting says.
.TP
.B \-\-window
Open the window even when
.B start\-in\-tray
is on.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-design
Ignore the design marked as the startup design for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-export-icons " directory"
Write the icon out as PNGs at 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 128 and 256 pixels and exit.
It needs no display, and it is what
.B make install
uses, so the icon in the icon theme is the same drawing as the window and the
panel icon rather than a second copy of it.
.SH STARTING IN THE PANEL
Turn on
.I "Start in the panel"
in the header, or run
.EX
claymore settings start-in-tray on
.EE
and the window stays away on every later start. That is the setting to enable
before adding
.B claymore-gui
to your desktop's autostart: the design is applied at login and no window
appears.
.PP
.B To panel
in the header moves the window out of the way for now, keeping the program
running, the design applied and the previews animating. The panel icon offers
.I "Show the window"
,
.IR "Re-apply my design" ,
.I "Hand the keyboard back"
and
.IR "Quit and keep the design" .
.PP
The panel icon is built on
.IR GtkStatusIcon ,
which needs a tray to attach to. On a desktop without one the window is left
open instead of the program disappearing where it cannot be reached.
.SH FILES
See
.BR claymore (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claymore (1)
